mprofile-kernel
Target Report Mask(PROFILE_KERNEL)
Call mcount for profiling before a function prologue

;  Select pointer size. This flag only used for CellOS Lv-2
;  Enable 64bit features, but address and pointer is handles in 32bit
;  space. This flag is asserted by -mp32 or -mlp32 option
mlp32
Target Report RejectNegative Mask(PPC64_LP32)
Generate codes in ILP32 model.(defualt)

;
mlp64
Target Report RejectNegative InverseMask(PPC64_LP32, PPC64_LP64)
Generate codes in LP64 model.

mp32
Target Report RejectNegative Mask(PPC64_LP32) MaskExists
same as -mlp32 option

mprxfixup
Target Report RejectNegative
Invoke ppu-lv2-prx-fixup after linking. This is default.

mno-prxfixup
Target Report RejectNegative
Does not invoke ppu-lv2-prx-fixup after linking. Special option for toolchain developer.

mprx
Target Report RejectNegative
Link objects in PRX mode.

mprx-with-runtime
Target Report RejectNegative
Link objects in PRX mode with the PRX runtime.

mlv2-stub
Target Report RejectNegative
Link with the lv2_stub.a library (even when using -mno-prxfixup)

msn-ld
Target Rerpot
Invoke SN linker instead of GNU binutils LD. This is default.

mforce-prx-fixup
Target Rerpot RejectNegative
Invoke ppu-lv2-fixup instead of oneramp linking built in SN LD. This is for debug perpose.
